{"agent_id":"pp3g-Qdw8-exp7-t5-freeze-plus-zero-spend-phase-a-zero-network","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:01:59.690391414Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"9ce478c3-f9e6-4a76-81c5-19432e9a547a","author":"pp3g-Qdw8-exp7-t5-freeze-plus-zero-spend-phase-a-zero-network","content":"Plan: Exp7 T5 — freeze + zero-spend Phase A (DESIGN §F, §G, §I). Zero network calls, zero measured Jev calls.\n\n## Inputs (read-only, frozen)\nThe phase2 tree does not exist in this worktree's checkout (HEAD 719223195 = main). It lives on branch `research/jev-phase1-565` @ 007095a75. I will materialise the input files at their canonical relative paths via `git archive research/jev-phase1-565 research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2 | tar -x` — extraction only, byte-identical to the committed blobs, nothing modified, nothing staged, and hidden from `git status` via .git/info/exclude so the commit can contain exactly the 3 requested paths. This mirrors the read-only git-show pattern used by the earlier recon on this issue but makes the pipeline actually runnable in place so the committed freeze.py is re-runnable.\n\n## Step 1 — freeze.py (new file, experiment7/freeze.py)\nRecords every result-affecting component with sha256 into experiment7/FREEZE.json: 8 corpus input refs + PROVENANCE, reuse_check.json, DESIGN.md, PRIMATIVES.md, BASELINE.md, REUSE-CHECK.md, build_packet.py, packet.json, run_noul.py, analyze.py, PACKET-CHECK.md, RUNNER-PROOF.md, SCORER-PROOF.md, AUDIT-PAIRS.md, and the freeze script itself. Also pins the frozen experiment6 inputs (packet.json must be sha256 1310c3d3…, results/exec.jsonl) and asserts read-only + unmodified (mode bits, mtime-vs-content, git blob sha equivalence). Subcommands: write (emit FREEZE.json), verify (re-hash all, FAIL on any drift).\n\n## Step 2 — zero-send construction-validation pipeline\n- python3 build_packet.py check\n- python3 run_noul.py plan  and  python3 run_noul.py proof\n- python3 analyze.py selfcheck\n- independent reconstruction of packet.json from frozen inputs → prove byte-identity against the frozen packet (expected sha c9598052)\n- prove planned cardinality exactly 48 rows / 24 pairs / 8 per stratum\n- prove all 48 outgoing payloads match the frozen packet\n- tamper controls against the key scientific invariants: pair swap, decisive-fact drop, question leak, polarity flip, resend-on-resume\n\n## Step 3 — freeze verified BEFORE and AFTER the checks\nAny drift between the two verifications fails the gate.\n\n## Step 4 — credential scan\nGrep all experiment7 artifacts + the three scripts for secret patterns; prove only the named locations (env var name TYPESAFE_API_KEY, --credential-file path) appear, never values.\n\n## Deliverables (commit ONLY these 3 paths on #574)\n1. research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/freeze.py\n2. research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/FREEZE.json\n3. research/jev-bounded-judgment/phase2/experiment7/PHASE-A.md\n\nPHASE-A.md carries per-gate PASS/FAIL, component count, freeze version, and an explicit measured-calls-equals-0 statement.\n\n## Constraints honoured\nNothing under experiment6/, no frozen packet, no builder/runner/scorer source, and no other file is modified. The only subcommand that can spend is run_noul.py run — it is never invoked.\n\n## Certainty\nPlan is evidence-based: I read DESIGN.md §§F/G/I and the CLI surfaces of build_packet.py, run_noul.py, analyze.py. NOT-TESTED until execution: whether the pipeline passes its own gates.","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:01:59.681580114Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:ysA8Ntd7onMFCreK2Fnm+JnK5KF1TUsnch/A0ci1z9c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4CkeeC+dK2ZKqbQVkOTqjJAvPQ+WlStOdsrcoGbpoL0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAzwFC6AennuVbsnnoDrjNXsfQMpSexvsX0236Ej76lsccRpmHI5Iy+GU7DxlL5S5tJjP6Mqx6U43pxwWjDvsWCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:ysA8Ntd7onMFCreK2Fnm+JnK5KF1TUsn