{"agent_id":"pp3g-Qdw8-exp7-t5-freeze-plus-zero-spend-phase-a-zero-network","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:30:22.266115186Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4ce2b6fe-caab-4f53-9a26-d55b1dcabc0e","comment_uuid":"71f2a136-8423-48bb-b916-72a9668e0561","author":"pp3g-Qdw8-exp7-t5-freeze-plus-zero-spend-phase-a-zero-network","content":"Result: Exp7 T5 Phase A — **PASS**. 8 gates, 8 green. Freeze version `exp7-freeze-1.0.0`, **30 components** across 11 roles. Committed as 6d9615994 on `feature/pp3g-Qdw8-exp7-t5-freeze-plus-zero-spend-phase-a-zero-network` — **exactly three paths** (freeze.py, FREEZE.json, PHASE-A.md).\n\n## Measured calls equals 0 — measured, not asserted\n**0 network events. 0 measured Jev calls. 0 network clients spawned.** `run_noul.py run` is the only subcommand that can spend; it was never invoked. The evidence is a `sitecustomize.py` audit hook on PYTHONPATH that CPython loads in the pipeline process **and in every child it spawns** (env is inherited). It records, without blocking, every network event, every write-mode open with its path, and every `subprocess.Popen` with its argv. A guard that raised would replace a real failure message with its own; a recorded zero states the same claim. Totals: 530 reads, 220 writes, 19 children (all python3, all in-tree), 0 network, 0 curl. `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` was also removed from the environment of every command, so the run could not authenticate even by accident.\n\n## Per-gate\n| Gate | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| freeze_before (30 components re-hashed) | PASS 0 findings |\n| exp6_read_only | PASS |\n| pipeline (5 zero-send commands + rebuild, all exit 0) | PASS |\n| reconstruct | PASS 13/13 |\n| payloads | PASS 9/9 |\n| tamper | PASS 6/6 |\n| credentials | PASS, 5/5 controls |\n| freeze_after (30 components re-hashed) | PASS 0 findings |\n\n## Experiment 6 read-only and unmodified — three independent grounds\n1. **Content** — packet.json sha256 1310c3d3c89c2070… (the pre-run pin); exec.jsonl b1ecc1cf985d899b…, 48 records.\n2. **Committed** — the git blob id **of the bytes on disk** equals the blob id committed at research/jev-phase1-565 for both files. An independent sweep of the whole extracted tree: **0 of 231** committed files differ from their blob.\n3. **Observed** — 220 write opens across the run, **0 under experiment6/**. Plus an AST scan of all four Exp7 modules: 50 write-capable calls, none naming an experiment6 path. AST not text, on purpose: run_noul.py contains the string experiment6 in its own docstrings and a text check would have fired on them.\n\n## Independent reconstruction\nTwo claims kept apart, because neither is the other. (a) *Determinism*: build_packet.py build reproduces packet.json byte-for-byte, sha256 **c959805273627089396f9f498d6b279e068a40a0472eec8d316edb5423b2d89a**. (b) *Independence*: freeze.py re-derives all 48 rows in its own code, importing nothing from build_packet.py, from the frozen Exp-6 packet + reuse_check.json + the Noul wording checked against DESIGN.md section D at run time. **0 field mismatches across 48 rows x 15 fields**; 24/24 twins differ only in the variant marker and the decisive fact; 48/48 request and state digests recomputed; 48/48 omit criteria; 48/48 name jev-1.13.0. The DESIGN-wording check discriminates — one reworded template makes it fail.\n\n## Cardinality\n**48 rows / 24 pairs / 8 pairs per stratum** (16 rows per stratum; the packet's counts.per_class counts pairs — stated because 8-per-stratum read as rows would be a different, wrong number). 48/48 outgoing states byte-identical to the frozen Exp-6 states; 48/48 payload hashes canonical; 48/48 distinct resume keys.\n\n## Tamper controls — 5/5 must-fail, no survivor\nEach control corrupts a copy, points a **real gate at that copy**, and requires a named rejection. Each first asserts the mutation actually changed bytes (RUNNER-PROOF 14b finding 10).\n- pair_swap (U/A relabel without swapping states — the sufficiency-experiment forgery) — check exit 5, plan exit 1, 4 checks failed\n- decisive_fact_drop — 8 checks failed\n- question_leak — check exit 5, plan exit 1, 5 checks failed\n- polarity_flip (scorer reads p_suff backwards; runs the MUTATED copy) — selfcheck exit 1, `FAIL polarity`\n- resend_on_resume (is_complete() success arm inverted; runs the MUTATED copy) — proof exit 1, resume 4/12\n- clean_baseline — must PASS, and does\n\n## Credential scan\n23 artifacts, **0 high-signal secrets, 0 high-entropy candidates**, 1 760 digest strings correctly classified as digests. Only named locations appear: TYPESAFE_API_KEY, --credential-env, --credential-file. 5/5 negative controls (4 injected secrets caught, 1 injected sha256 correctly NOT flagged). The patterns are split high-signal vs generic-entropy because one pattern matches all 1 760 digests here; generic matching runs over LOGICAL strings (AST / JSON parser) so a digest split across two source lines counts once. **One reviewed exception, disclosed not suppressed**: run_noul.py:2992 `secret = \"FIXTURE-SECRET-abc123-not-a-real-key\"` — the runner's own zero-send credential proof fixture, temp file, never sent. The only such literal in 23 files. Injected control secrets are assembled from fragments so the scan does not report its own fixture.\n\n## Finding (NOT repaired — repairing it would edit a frozen document)\n**PACKET-CHECK.md is byte-reproducible only modulo the absolute worktree path it records.** The pipeline is run with --check-out/--out redirected to scratch precisely so the frozen proof documents are re-derived and COMPARED rather than overwritten. RUNNER-PROOF.md: byte-identical. PACKET-CHECK.md: 4 differing lines (261-264), all the provenance origin column, every digest/size/blob/count identical. The committed copy was produced in .worktrees/jev-phase1; this ran in .worktrees/pp3g-Qdw8-…. Normalisation is narrow: it rewrites only an absolute prefix ending at the phase-2 root, reports which line numbers differed, and requires every differing line to contain that path — a real content change fails the gate.\n\n## What this does NOT establish\nNothing about H1, H2, or any scientific result: no number exists yet. Not tested: that jev-1.13.0 accepts this body or what it would answer; the live Retry-After shape; the answer key; that a live credential resolves; whether the Exp-6 question is the right thing to ask a sufficiency Noul about (DESIGN section H, a STOP gate, not re-adjudicated). Carried forward unrepaired: 4 attribute-receiver pairs without independent reachability proof, 2 calendar pairs under P2b over-approximation.\n\n## ENVIRONMENT (needs operator action)\nThe phase-2 tree does not exist on this branch (HEAD 719223195 = main). Inputs were materialised read-only at their canonical paths via `git archive research/jev-phase1-565` and hidden from git status with a marked block in .git/info/exclude (remove it when the worktree is discarded). Nothing under experiment6/ was modified — verified by digest, by blob identity and by an observed zero-write trace. **Merging this branch into research/jev-phase1-565 is still required for the three deliverables to land next to experiment6/; that merge and any push are operator-gated, so I have not performed them.**\n\n## Certainty\n- WHY: a freeze is worth having only if drift fails it, and a zero-spend claim is worth reading only if measured — so every claim is a named re-hash, a recorded audit-hook counter, or a mutation proven to change bytes before the gate was asked to reject it.\n- WHAT: deterministic re-derivation from four frozen inputs; byte-identity rebuild; an observed write/network trace of every process started; AST+regex scan of 23 artifacts. stdlib only, no network.\n- HOW CERTAIN: **proven** for construction/validation (cardinality, byte-identity, drift-freedom, zero network, zero measured calls, all five invariants rejected under mutation). **Not proven, out of scope** for anything about the scientific result.\n- WHAT-NOT-TESTED: section 10 of PHASE-A.md in full. Sharpest omission: this proves the machine that would run Exp7 is correct and idle. It says nothing about whether Exp7 will find anything.\n\n## Artifacts\n- experiment7/freeze.py (2 029 lines) sha256 c438232172b8909b81b2a2050efb209781f7f7f3bddbfa550b948fa805465ad4\n- experiment7/FREEZE.json (360 lines) sha256 9715cfdbe58ccc3c38e709da96dcad291b6195f9e3980f0a429a36d9e7703966\n- experiment7/PHASE-A.md (427 lines) sha256 42bb9c611f0312083500a2c807009cd989234c9e22c56d446e27520434b997a0","created_at":"2026-09-29T15:30:22.258623699Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:ysA8Ntd7onMFCreK2Fnm+JnK5KF1TUsnch/A0ci1z9c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4CkeeC+dK2ZKqbQVkOTqjJAvPQ+WlStOdsrcoGbpoL0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAbOqlWFPpX2fzLsSXd2jogpA9HUPckBjOGBmvnjYkY+nPjLsrk4mhiz1W5LbxS50qDxVqbpGURU8KRxTjBiJSBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:ysA8Ntd7onMFCreK2Fnm+JnK5KF1TUsnch/A0ci1z9c","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4CkeeC+dK2ZKqbQVkOTqjJAvPQ+WlStOdsrcoGbpoL0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQODP+1QCDNnQQVS2MPfH3iYSSx+2tbOPLfcZArogAtqFaZ2wCJZvZJpFpjb7anZcFNEu5UQQ3/nnRBC0erU+lQA="}
